---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
---

<Layout title="About — Trainory" description="Why Trainory exists: a small, free protein tracker and workout planner built by one person to replace a training plan kept in a notes app.">
  <article class="prose-page">
    <h1>About Trainory</h1>
    <p>Trainory started as a page in a notes app: a four-day training split, a list of meals, and a line that said "120 g of protein a day". The plan was fine. What was missing was any way of knowing whether it was being followed.</p>
    <p>So this site turns that page into something you can tick off. It shows today's workout and how much protein is left, lets you log both in a few taps, and keeps the history so you can see whether the weights and your body weight are moving in the right direction.</p>

    <h2>What it is</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A protein tracker that counts grams of protein and nothing else.</li>
      <li>A workout planner where every workout, exercise, photo and rest time is yours to edit.</li>
      <li>Reports built from your own logs: protein per day, consistency, strength and body weight.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What it is not</h2>
    <p>It is not a calorie counter, a coaching service or medical advice. The starter plan is an example to edit, not a prescription. Talk to a doctor or a qualified coach before changing your diet or training if you have a health condition.</p>

    <h2>Who makes it</h2>
    <p>Trainory is built and maintained by {SITE.creator}. Questions, bug reports and feature ideas are welcome at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
    <p>Exercise photos and instructions in the starter plan come from the public-domain <a href="https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db" rel="noopener">free-exercise-db</a> project.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
